1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,480
 So one of the most common questions that I get asked

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:05,960
 when I show the demo of agentic AI application

3
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:09,320
 is that it does not generate anything.

4
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:12,360
 So how can this be a generative AI application?

5
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:14,080
 And the answer to that question is

6
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,220
 that agentic AI is not generative AI.

7
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:19,760
 They are both different.

8
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:22,560
 And sometimes the reason why people confuse

9
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:24,600
 between generative AI and agentic AI

10
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,720
 is that they both use a large language model.

11
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:32,280
 But that's probably the only similarity between the two.

12
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:33,840
 Now let's go and take a look

13
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:37,560
 at what's the difference between generative and agentic AI.

14
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:40,680
 Now let's start with what is a focus of both.

15
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:45,120
 For generative AI, the focus is on content generation.

16
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:46,880
 So whether you want to generate text,

17
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:50,720
 images, code, you will use generative AI.

18
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:54,640
 But the focus area for agentic AI is to execute

19
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:59,640
 complex tasks autonomously with minimal human intervention.

20
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:03,040
 Now let's try and understand this through a use case.

21
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:04,800
 So let's say you have a human developer

22
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,480
 and you want to improve his productivity.

23
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:11,080
 So what you will do is you will build a generative AI application

24
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:13,240
 such as a code generator through which

25
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:17,360
 it can generate code from a natural language query.

26
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,840
 Now let's assume there's a production defect

27
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:24,160
 and he analyzes the issue and then pulls a query

28
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:28,400
 to the generative AI app to generate some code for it

29
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:30,720
 so that you can fix the defect.

30
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:32,000
 So it will generate the code.

31
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,680
 You will implement the code at test the code

32
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:35,800
 and then it will be good.

33
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:38,280
 So it has improves his productivity.

34
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:41,600
 Now let's take the same use case on how it will be implemented

35
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:43,520
 through the agentic AI.

36
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,920
 So here you will build a developer agent

37
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:50,080
 and you will not require human intervention.

38
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:53,000
 Or at least you will require minimal human intervention.

39
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,520
 So what this developer agent will do is

40
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:57,880
 so it will evaluate the logs

41
00:01:57,880 --> 00:02:00,160
 and understand what the defect is.

42
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:01,760
 Then based on the evaluation of the logs,

43
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,120
 it will generate code.

44
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:08,120
 It will update the code, test it out and implement it.

45
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:10,760
 So it will do everything by itself

46
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:13,960
 and would not require the human intervention.

47
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:16,920
 Maybe you can keep the human in loop at the end.

48
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:19,960
 Once the code has been generated, update it, test it.

49
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,480
 Then just before the implementation,

50
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:24,000
 you can have a human in loop who will review

51
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,360
 and then implement.

52
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:29,800
 Next, generative AI can also act as a productivity enhancer.

53
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,400
 So maybe you will have a generative AI application

54
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:34,160
 that can do the content creation

55
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:37,600
 such as press briefings, creation of videos,

56
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,760
 brochures for the marketing team.

57
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:42,440
 On the other hand, for agentic AI,

58
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:46,160
 a great use case would be a customer service chatbot

59
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:49,640
 that can answer the complex user queries

60
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:51,520
 by understanding the user queries

61
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:54,000
 and then retrieving the relevant data

62
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,880
 from relational, non-relational, or ragged-based solutions

63
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:01,280
 and give a response back to the end user.

64
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,720
 Now let's take a look at the capabilities

65
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:06,080
 and limitation of generative and agentic AI.

66
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:09,120
 So the problem is the only similarity between generative

67
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:11,880
 and agentic AI is that they are both powered

68
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:14,520
 by a large language model.

69
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,280
 So you could have clawed, lamothree, open AI,

70
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,320
 or any other LLM.

71
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:22,120
 Next, generative AI is limited to the training data

72
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,240
 of the LLM.

73
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:26,160
 So whatever data the LLM has been trained on,

74
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:30,360
 it can answer questions only related to its training data.

75
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:33,520
 It also does not have access to real-time data

76
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:35,200
 or enterprise data.

77
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,560
 So let's say for LLM,

78
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:40,680
 the training was completed on June 2023.

79
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:43,560
 So any event happening after that date,

80
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:47,160
 the LLM would not be able to answer those questions.

81
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:50,240
 So it cannot also tell you, what is the weather like today

82
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:51,240
 in New York?

83
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:55,480
 Because it has no access to real-time or enterprise data.

84
00:03:55,480 --> 00:04:00,200
 On the other hand, agentic AI can integrate with enterprise

85
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:03,600
 data sources, relational, non-relational, vector DB.

86
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:05,320
 It can also access real-time data

87
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:09,400
 such as weather data, hotel booking, flight booking,

88
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:11,920
 because it can integrate with tools

89
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:14,840
 that can make an API call to the backend systems

90
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:18,600
 and get you the real-time or enterprise data.

91
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:21,400
 Then large language models are stateless.

92
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:22,800
 They have no memory.

93
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:26,000
 So you can enable memory in a generative applications,

94
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,200
 maybe through LinkedIn where you can enable conversation,

95
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:34,200
 buffer memory, but by default, it does not have any memory.

96
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:36,120
 While as in the agentic AI,

97
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:39,520
 you will have a long-term and short-term memory

98
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:43,600
 to contextualize and personalize the response

99
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,560
 to the user.

100
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:48,680
 Genity AI also does not have any reasoning capability

101
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:51,320
 through which it can break down the user request

102
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:53,440
 into multiple tasks.

103
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:57,280
 Well, as that capability is available with the agentic AI

104
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:59,760
 where it will evaluate the user request

105
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:03,200
 and break it down into smaller, subtask

106
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,960
 using the large language model.

107
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:08,160
 Now let's go ahead and take a look at a common architecture

108
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:10,720
 for Genity AI-based application.

109
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:13,240
 So we'll have a front end through which the user would send

110
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:16,640
 his queries, then maybe you will have a rest API,

111
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:19,680
 maybe a Lambda function, and then Amazon bedrock

112
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:22,600
 and some underlying foundational model.

113
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,680
 Now in case of agentic AI,

114
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:26,680
 you will have a large language model

115
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:29,000
 that will be driving the agent.

116
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,720
 Then it will have some tools.

117
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:33,320
 Let's say Lambda function, maybe knowledge bases,

118
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:35,960
 which will query the backend systems

119
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:39,240
 and get the data for the HR agent.

120
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:42,120
 It will have a memory to contextualize and personalize

121
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,080
 the responses.

122
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:44,560
 It will have some guardrails.

123
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:47,680
 Then if you're also building multi agent applications,

124
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,800
 you will need orchestration framework,

125
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:53,360
 such as Amazon bedrock multi agent orchestration framework,

126
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:56,480
 land graph, crew AI, and so on.

127
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:59,880
 So how would a typical Genity AI application work?

128
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:02,640
 So let's say you have a user who's doing to generate

129
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:07,320
 some content, he will send that request or prompt

130
00:06:07,320 --> 00:06:10,840
 via AWS API gateway to a Lambda function.

131
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:14,080
 And then this Lambda function is going to enhance

132
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:17,560
 the user input with a prompt template.

133
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:21,760
 And then send that request to Amazon bedrock

134
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:24,880
 and Amazon bedrock will further send that request

135
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:28,000
 to a foundation model, then it will generate a response

136
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,840
 and send it back to the user.

137
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:33,800
 So in case of agentic application, how would that work?

138
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:37,120
 So you will have a user that will send that request

139
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:40,600
 to an agent, then agent is going to break down

140
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:43,600
 the user task into multiple steps.

141
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:46,600
 And then it will use the tools that it has

142
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:49,160
 maybe a Lambda function, maybe a better

143
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:52,720
 on knowledge base to retrieve the data from the backend.

144
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:57,480
 And once it gets a response back from these backend systems,

145
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,520
 it's going to consolidate that input

146
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:02,240
 and send it back to the user.

147
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:04,040
 So this is some key differences between

148
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:07,240
 generative and agentic AI. I hope you like this lecture. Thank you.

